      "message": "IIUC, this workflow can be realized using the current implementation as well, albeit the mirror opposite (i.e. we can set BUILD_BROKEN_SRC_DIR_IS_RO :\u003d true on some products to catch generic issues)\n\nMy reasoning for preferring BUILD_BROKEN_SRC_DIR_IS_RO over BUILD_BROKEN_SRC_DIR_IS_WRITABLE is\n```\nBy default, this boolean env var will be missing in all of our product_configs. Unset booleans are considered \"falsy\" in many languages. Defaulting missing BUILD_BROKEN_SRC_DIR_IS_RO to false ensures that this CL would not change the existing RW nature of the source tree\n```\n\nWill inverting it to BUILD_BROKEN_SRC_DIR_IS_WRITABLE align it how we use BUILD_BROKEN_* flags during builds? I am a Noogler so it is likely that I might be missing some nuances",
